// Title: Suspicious Get-Variable.exe Creation
// Sigma ID: 0c3fac91-5627-46e8-a6a8-a0d7b9b8ae1b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, stealth, T1546, T1027
// Description: Get-Variable is a valid PowerShell cmdlet WindowsApps is by default in the path where PowerShell
//   is executed. So when the Get-Variable command is issued on PowerShell execution, the system
//   first looks for the Get-Variable executable in the path and executes the malicious binary
//   instead of looking for the PowerShell cmdlet.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.malwarebytes.com/threat-intelligence/2022/04/colibri-loader-combines-task-scheduler-and-powershell-in-clever-persistence-technique/
//   - https://www.joesandbox.com/analysis/465533/0/html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_get_variable.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "Local\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps\\Get-Variable.exe"
